**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The kit files that exist many times, one verb set for every kind (001 §A 'The kit root is flat: every kit file sits at the root, and its kind is its extension'; the S4.1 brief: list, read, write and delete kit files per kind, generic over the kind's extension so later kinds add no verbs). (1) `KitProxy` (step 125) gains four fields, each with a one-line doc. `listKindFiles : KitFileKind -> Result<FileStem list, KitError>` answers the stems of the files at the kit root whose names end with the kind's extension (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`), in ordinal order; a file of another kind, the `.kit-json`, a `*.tmp` and a file in a subfolder are not listed. `readKindFile : KitFileKind -> FileStem -> Result<KitFileText, KitError>` answers the text of `kind.fileNameOf stem` (step 123), or `MissingKitFileErr` naming it. `writeKindFile : KitFileKind -> FileStem -> KitFileText -> Result<unit, KitError>` creates or replaces that file whole. `deleteKindFile : KitFileKind -> FileStem -> Result<unit, KitError>` deletes it, or answers `MissingKitFileErr` naming it and changes nothing. The stem is the caller's, made safe by step 24's rule (`FileStem.ofText`) before the call, so a name keeps the lab's characters (.spec-md §3.11). The text is the caller's; each kind's format arrives with its shapes, as the kit file's did in step 124. (2) `KitProxy.createInMemory` (step 125) implements them over the folder's one map of texts, at the root path `kind.fileNameOf stem`. (3) `KitProxy.create` (step 126) implements them over the folder's root: the listing reads the folder's top-level file names; a read decodes UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark dropped; a write goes through `writeBytesAtomically` (step 126) as UTF-8 without a byte-order mark; IO exceptions are `KitIoErr` as in step 126. Tests. New `KitProxyContract` facts (step 125), so both classes run them: `kit files of every kind are listed, read, replaced and deleted by their names`: after `initialiseKit`, for each kind of `KitFileKind.all`, `writeKindFile` of the stems `QZ-LR` and `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL` with distinct texts, then `listKindFiles` answers the two in ordinal order, `readKindFile` answers each text, a second `writeKindFile` of `QZ-LR` replaces its text, and `deleteKindFile` of the other leaves `listKindFiles` answering `QZ-LR` alone; files of the other kinds and the `.kit-json` are never listed under a kind, and `paths` holds each file at its name. `reading or deleting a missing kit file is MissingKitFileErr and changes nothing`: `readKindFile` and `deleteKindFile` of a stem never written answer `MissingKitFileErr`, and `paths` is unchanged. `replacing a kit file leaves only its new text and no temporary file`: after `writeKindFile` of `QZ-LR` as a setup and its replacement, `paths` holds `QZ-LR.setup-json` once and no path ending with `.tmp`, and `readKindFile` answers the new text. `KitProxyFolderTests` gains `a replace that fails keeps the old file whole, removes its temporary file and is KitIoErr`: while the test holds `QZ-LR.setup-json` open with `FileShare.None`, `writeKindFile` of a new text answers `KitIoErr`; once the test lets go, the file holds its old text and the folder holds no `*.tmp`.

**Acceptance.** After the per-kind verbs land, both `KitProxy` implementations MUST list, read, write and delete kit files of every `KitFileKind` by stem; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `kit files of every kind are listed, read, replaced and deleted by their names`, `reading or deleting a missing kit file is MissingKitFileErr and changes nothing`, `replacing a kit file leaves only its new text and no temporary file` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests` and `a replace that fails keeps the old file whole, removes its temporary file and is KitIoErr`, the count rising by 7; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.
